			"description": "| **Endpoint** | **Description** |\n| --- | --- |\n| GET `/customers` | Get all customers available |\n| GET `/customers/{customerId}` | Get a customer by id |\n| POST `/customers` | Create a new customer. If the customer data is valid it should echo the request body, else it should return a exception message with type `InvalidInputException` |\n| PUT `/customer/{customerId}` | Update a customer with new data. If the customer data is valid it should echo the request body, else it should return a exception message with type `InvalidInputException` |\n| DELETE `/customers/{customerId}` | Deletes a customer. In case of a invalid customer id, a `CustomerNotFoundException` should be expected. |\n\nThe schema for a customer JSON object is given below;\n\n``` json\n{\n    \"firstName\": \"<First-Name>\",\n    \"lastName\": \"<Last-Name>\",\n    \"email\": \"<Email-Address>\",\n    \"password\": \"<Password>\"\n}\n\n ```"
